WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here´s what people
are talking about.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it´s still this speech
Senator Jeff Flake gave

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.505 size:81% position:41%
about Trump yesterday.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yep, he criticized Trump
for 20 minutes

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.444
without mentioning him by name,
but I think people knew

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.114
who he meant when he kept
referring to Tweety McTweetface.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tweety McTweet --

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.086
Trump was tweeting again today.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.055
He said that his big meeting
with republican senators was

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
a love fest with multiple
standing ovations.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.694
Yep, they were mostly people
getting up to leave, but still,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
that counts as
a standing ovation.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-Standing.

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:34.834
-Trump sent three tweets
about how the senators gave him

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
a standing ovation.
It´s a big deal for Trump.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
He hasn´t seen 50 people
cheering him on since

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:39.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
his inauguration.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
But today, when
he was talking to reporters,

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.680
Trump said that he has one
of the greatest memories

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all time.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.985
Then Trump said, [ As Trump ]
"And if you don´t believe me,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
ask my sons Derek
and Ron Junior.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.094
And my daughter, girl Donald."

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ] Girl Donald?
That´s not a -- What?

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
Girl Donald?
That´s not a name.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.938
Trump also spent a few minutes
talking about how he´s portrayed

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the media.
Listen to what he says.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i>-Well, I think the press makes
me more uncivil than I am.</i>

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i>You know,
people don´t understand,</i>

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i>I went to an
Ivy-League College.</i>

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.184 size:78% position:39% line:0%
<i>I was a nice student.</i>

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.019 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i>I did very well.</i>

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:29.289 line:0%
<i>I´m a very intelligent person.</i>

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.060 size:78% position:39%
-I mean, nothing says
"I´m smart" better

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
than shouting it
on your front lawn.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Trump ] "I´m very smart.
[ Applause ]

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
You, kid on the bike,
I´m smart."

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.837 size:84% position:42%
[ Normal voice ] Okay,
we´re good, we´re good.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Get this.
I read that President Trump

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:51.544
wanted to change the name
of a mountain in Alaska,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.780
but the state senators said no.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.682 size:88% position:44%
Yeah, it turns out that
Trump has a lot of other

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
famous landmarks he´s offered
to rename as well.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.319
I´ll show you what I mean.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.754
For example, Trump offered
to rename the Grand Canyon

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
the "Bigly Hole."

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:03.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Next up, Trump offered
to rename the Liberty Bell,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.297
the "Taco Bell Monument."

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.602 size:75% position:38%
[ As Trump ] Quiero.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ] And finally,
Trump offered to rename

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
the U.S. Capitol Building
the "Yuge Boob."

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you go --
What are you doing?

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-They´re not going to work.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.178 size:78% position:39%
Don´t worry about it.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.147
And we all know Halloween
is right around the corner

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.449
and many people still haven´t
picked out their costumes,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
so here with a few suggestions
is our own "Tonight Show"

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
Halloween correspondent,
Julio Torres,

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.188 size:78% position:39%
ladies and gentlemen.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:38.391 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
Great crowd, Julio Torres.
-Hi.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.063 size:84% position:42%
Hi, hi, hello, and boo.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.167 size:84% position:42%
-Julio, I understand
you have ideas for some

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.768
last-minute Halloween costumes?

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, correct.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.405
If you´re struggling to find
a costume, how about something

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
easy like --

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.176 line:0%
like the Lost City of Atlantis.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:03:01.548 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.316 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-That sounds like more of
a concept.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:06.152 line:0%
How about something like a --
like a ghost, like a ghost.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.387 size:81% position:41% line:0%
-Oh, sure, sure, sure.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
How about a Ferrero Rocher
chocolate.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:15.762 line:0%
Or -- Or an e-mail forward from
your dad.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.764 --> 00:03:19.866 line:0%
Or a raccoon foolishly wearing

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.301 line:0%
all the diamonds he stole.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:29.676 size:84% position:42% line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:30.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-What?

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.245 size:88% position:44% line:0%
-Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Okay, how about a cashier
from Chipotle

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.217 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
catching you putting soda into
the water cup and going,

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
"You <i>lied </i>to me."

00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Applause ]

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:45.425 line:0%
-What about costumes for people
are more familiar with.

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:48.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Like, how about a Dracula or
"Deadpool"?

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:52.232 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-Who?
-Dracula, "Deadpool"?

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:55.235 line:0%
-You could also be a turtle who
just told off another turtle

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:58.404 line:0%
and now it has to turn away
and storm off very slowly.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.040 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.377 line:0%
Or a statue who came to life but
now has a job

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.145 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
and a family and misses the
simple days

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.480 size:81% position:41% line:0%
of just being admired.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.949 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.851 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-Julio, I have to say, I love
these costumes.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.586 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
They all seem pretty
high-concept.

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.221 line:0%
Is there something you can
recommend that´s a little

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:18.491 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
simpler for people who aren´t
as creative?

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.994 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-Well, you can always be the
Tooth Fairy being like,

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.162 line:0%
"Dear God, I can´t afford to buy
more teeth.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.631 line:0%
What do I even do with these?"

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:27.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:31.604 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Or -- Or how about St. Peter
welcoming someone who was

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
anti-immigration to Heaven
and being like,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.842 line:0%
"Oh, no, you forgot the forms.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.444 line:0%
Now you have to wait in line.
I´m sorry, rules are rules."

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:41.114 size:84% position:42% line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-Julio, what about something
super simple?

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.520 line:0%
-Yeah, I mean, I´m personally
torn between being a secret

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.821 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
or a rumor.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:52.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:56.729 line:0%
-I meant like a football player
or something.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-What? But I´m --
I´m not a football player.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.834 line:0%
Like, would I have to, like, put
on a bunch of weight?

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.170 size:88% position:44% line:0%
That´s -- That´s insane.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i>-That´s </i>insane?

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.941 line:0%
-Season six of "One Tree Hill."

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:15.581 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Or -- Or a telegram that never
arrived that would

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.749 line:0%
have made all the difference.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:23.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:27.260 size:78% position:39% line:0%
Or -- Or, wait, wait,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.063 line:0%
how about a nice green tea
from Starbucks that was supposed

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.964 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
to be unsweetened,
but it´s sweetened

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
so now it´s up for grabs if
anyone wants it.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:39.706 size:78% position:39% line:0%
-Anyone could take --

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
-I mean, you can always go as
maybe like a flamingo

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.409 line:0%
that´s like, "You know what?

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.610 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I´m just going to use
both legs."

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.047 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you very much.
I appreciate that.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
those are my suggestions.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.050
Enjoy being a football player.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.585 size:88% position:44%
-Julio Torres, everyone.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.153 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s up for grabs.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
My neck hurts.
My neck hurts from laughing.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my goodness.
Good suggestions right there.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
Julio Torres once again.
How great is that?

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:10.169 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.304
Oh, check this out, guys,

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that one
of Albert Einstein´s notes

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
about his theory for
a happy life sold at auction

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:18.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
for $1.5 million.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience ohs ]
$1.5 million.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.849
It got awkward when the buyer
read the note and it said,

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.317
"Money can´t buy happiness."

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:29.455 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally,
I read that there are

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.859
some new airport security
measures starting this week

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:36.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and airlines can conduct short
interviews with passengers.

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:38.264
Most airlines will ask
the purpose of your trip,

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:40.800
while Spirit Airlines will ask
if you know how to land a plane.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight!
Give it up for the Roots!

